.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for lines containing a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.B int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep
function searches the supplied file stream for lines containing
.I search_str.
.PP
Matching lines are stored in a dynamically allocated array of strings and the
address of that array is returned through
.I matches.
.PP
The function returns the number of matching lines, or -1 if an invalid argument
is supplied or memory allocation fails.
